// Layer_Observability — Observability Layer (layer 7 of 9)
// Manual render: https://app.eraser.io > Diagram-as-code (cloud architecture).
//   Create a NEW canvas named "Layer_Observability".
// Export the PNG to materials/reports/figures/Layer_Observability.png
// Icons: product logos from docs.eraser.io/docs/icons (checked 2026-07-11):
//   prometheus, tempo, grafana, superset, clickhouse, trino; the rest use generic
//   icons (no flame icon exists in the list, so Pyroscope uses gauge).
//   OpenCost <> Prometheus is factually two-way: OpenCost reads usage metrics
//   from Prometheus and exports cost metrics that Prometheus scrapes
//   (OpenCost documentation).
// Reference: subsec:lapisan-observabilitas (Section IV.3, sec:arsitektur-terintegrasi);
//   tool detail for the layer on row 7 of tab:layanan_industri,
//   detailing the service group in Figure fig:integrate-service (Section IV.1).
//   Included in LaTeX as fig:layer-observability.
// Focus: OpenTelemetry collects signals into Grafana Tempo (traces), Prometheus
//   (metrics, with Alertmanager + Pushgateway), and Loki (logs); Grafana unifies
//   all three; Sloth translates SLO rules into Prometheus; Pyroscope profiles;
//   OpenCost computes cost; Superset serves analytics dashboards from ClickHouse
//   and Trino.
// Rendering MUST be horizontal (direction right): signals flow left to right into Grafana,
//   at most two node rows per group, so the diagram spreads wide and fits the band
//   height=0.42\textheight. Included without \rotatebox in LaTeX.
// Layer grounding: the group label carries its source category (najafabadi2024analysis),
//   namely monitoring components.
// Implementation check: nodes exist under platform/components/observability/
//   (opentelemetry, tempo, kube-prometheus-stack = Prometheus + Alertmanager,
//   pushgateway, loki, grafana, sloth, pyroscope, opencost) and data-processing/superset.

direction right

// Signal producer (boundary)
Platform Workload [icon: layers, color: gray, label: "Platform Workload (data, feature, model)"]

// Observability section
Observability Layer [icon: monitor, color: teal, label: "Observability Layer (monitoring category)"] {
  OpenTelemetry [icon: radio, label: "OpenTelemetry (collector)"]
  Prometheus [icon: prometheus, label: "Prometheus (+ Alertmanager + Pushgateway)"]
  Loki [icon: file-text, label: "Loki (logs)"]
  Tempo [icon: tempo, label: "Grafana Tempo (traces)"]
  Pyroscope [icon: gauge, label: "Pyroscope (continuous profiling)"]
  Sloth [icon: sliders, label: "Sloth (SLO rules)"]
  OpenCost [icon: dollar-sign, label: "OpenCost (cost)"]
  Grafana [icon: grafana, label: "Grafana (operational dashboard)"]
  Superset [icon: superset, label: "Apache Superset (analytics dashboard)"]
}

// Analytics sources and consumer (boundary)
ClickHouse [icon: clickhouse, color: green, label: "ClickHouse (analytics source)"]
Trino [icon: trino, color: orange, label: "Trino (federated query)"]
Business User [icon: user, color: gray, label: "Business User"]

// Signal collection flow
Platform Workload > OpenTelemetry: metrics + logs + traces
Platform Workload > Pyroscope: continuous profiling
OpenTelemetry > Prometheus: metrics
OpenTelemetry > Loki: logs
OpenTelemetry > Tempo: traces
Sloth > Prometheus: SLO rules

// Unification in Grafana
Prometheus > Grafana: metrics
Loki > Grafana: logs
Tempo > Grafana: traces
Pyroscope > Grafana: profiles
OpenCost <> Prometheus: usage and cost metrics
OpenCost > Grafana: cost per workload
Grafana > Business User: operational dashboard

// BI analytics flow
ClickHouse > Superset: analytics source
Trino > Superset: federated source
Superset > Business User: analytics dashboard
